  "run": {
    "final_text": "I added a v2.4.0 section to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, using the format of the earlier entries:\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * CSV export for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads on HTTP 503 with backoff (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when the config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in the monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\n- **Version and date:** these come from the `VERSION` and `RELEASE_DATE` files.\n- **ACME-421 left out:** I dropped it as you asked. It was the only change marked `!` (breaking: it removed the `--legacy` flag from sync). Since it was reverted, `--legacy` should still work in 2.4.0, so the notes don't need a breaking-changes or migration section.\n- **No contributor credits:** the earlier entries don't name authors, so I left out the `@` handles. I can add them if you want credits this time.",
